  "worked_solution": "The variable $z$ is being *multiplied* by $6.$ To isolate $z,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $6.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6z & >-5 \\\\ \\frac{6z}{6} & >\\frac{-5}{6} \\\\ \\frac{6z}{6} & >-\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $6$ from the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6z}{6} & >-\\frac{5}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{6}z}{\\cancel{6}} & >-\\frac{5}{6} \\\\ z & >-\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z>-\\frac{5}{6}.$",
